    config={'tex':{'inlineMath':[[r'\(',r'\)']],'displayMath':[[r'\[',r'\]']]},'options':{'skipHtmlTags':['script','style','pre','code']}}
    css='''main{max-width:1280px}.pass{padding:18px;background:#edf6ec;border-left:5px solid #447845}.controls{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:24px;margin:20px 0}.tile-line{display:grid;grid-template-columns:220px minmax(0,1fr);gap:24px;align-items:start;padding:20px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #d4dcd2}.square{aspect-ratio:1;box-sizing:border-box;padding:12px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:space-around;background:white;border:2px solid #4c654d;border-radius:4px;font-size:14px}.blue-layer{color:#174e9a;background:#edf4ff;border-left:4px solid #4e82c1;padding:5px}.purple-layer{color:#693791;background:#f3edff;border-left:4px solid #7954aa;padding:5px}.row-text{min-width:0}.math{display:inline-block;max-width:100%;overflow:auto;vertical-align:middle}.row-text>.math{font-size:18px}pre{font-size:12px;max-height:340px;overflow:auto;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}[hidden]{display:none!important}.tracks{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:14px}.tracks article{background:#f4f7ef;padding:17px;border:1px solid #d2dbcc}.tracks h3{font-size:18px}@media(max-width:700px){.tile-line{grid-template-columns:1fr}.square{width:220px}.tracks{grid-template-columns:1fr}}'''
    page='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Cluster-assisted incidence proof · GCTS research</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../report.css"><script>window.MathJax='+json.dumps(config)+';</script><script defer src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-chtml.js"></script><style>'+css+'</style></head><body><header class="masthead"><a href="../#fixed-family-search">Research report</a><span>NOTEBOOK 110</span><a href="#reader">Proof tiles</a></header><main>'
    deck='Automatic receptor binding and shared cluster expansion produce a checked recipient derivation under the original finite search budget.' if accepted else 'Automatic receptor binding and shared cluster expansion produce a complete recipient candidate under the original finite search budget.'
    page+='<section class="intro"><p class="eyebrow">ACTUAL CLUSTER-ASSISTED SEARCH · SYMBOLIC HILBERT INCIDENCE</p><h1>'+title+'</h1><p class="deck">'+deck+'</p><p><a href="#results">Actual result</a> · <a href="#reader">Tiles, formulas and English</a> · <a href="#comparison">Comparison</a> · <a href="#cost">Full costs</a></p></section>'
    page+='<section class="panel" id="results"><h2>A concrete incidence statement.</h2><p class="pass">'+assertion+'</p><p>The original hypotheses state that distinct points '+math('P,Q')+' lie on both '+math('l,m')+' and on both '+math('m,n')+', with the stated point and line sort guards. The third hypothesis is '+math(r'\operatorname{Incident}(R,l)')+'. The conclusion is '+math(r'\operatorname{Incident}(R,n)')+'. The selected rows apply guarded line uniqueness and equality substitution. All three hypotheses remain in the context.</p>'+stats+'<p>The complete graph executes one primitive placement at a time. Its global forced moves interrupt hint ordering. One hint retires when it becomes incompatible; the remaining immutable pool keeps full primitive fallback. This successful tape has no failed child, exclusion or rollback event, so it does not newly exercise those runtime paths.</p></section>'
    page+='<section class="panel" id="comparison"><h2>A positive result where the primitive controls remain unknown.</h2>'+comparison+'<p>All lanes retain the same original finite point model, hypotheses, '+math(24)+' rows, complete primitive domain, global scheduler, '+math(128)+'-attempt cap, '+math(20)+'-second search cap and '+math(2000)+'-event cap. A budget-limited control remains unknown. It does not establish that the control cannot find this proof with more resources.</p><p>This is evidence that reusable cluster hints help this instance. It is one observation with a fixed inventory, not a repeated speed comparison or evidence of superiority to established automated provers. Preparation and independent checking are charged below; the search clock alone is not a time-to-verified-proof cost.</p></section>'
    page+='<section class="panel" id="reader"><h2>Read the actual selected tiles line by line.</h2><p>These translation-only squares show the saved actual placements, in proof-row order. Blue markings carry formula codes and required formulas at distant source rows. Purple markings carry ordered source offsets. The formula beside each square decodes its primitive command; English explains the inference. Source links jump to the referenced rows.</p><p>This is a Wang-style point-marking adaptation with extended marking support. Native finite Wang adjacency acceptance is not invoked. Point, line and incidence are symbolic predicates; no geometric drawing supplies a proof step.</p><div class="controls"><label><input id="blue" type="checkbox" checked> Blue formula markings</label><label><input id="purple" type="checkbox" checked> Purple source offsets</label></div><div id="proof-view" aria-live="polite"></div></section>'
    page+='<section class="panel" id="assessment"><h2>What GCTS contributes here.</h2><p>The useful step is automatic composition: the full existing '+math(171)+'-family inventory yielded '+math(5)+' compatible single or paired proposals through exact receptor binding. Shared primitive placements count once. The search used these whole unions as preferences and constructed the recipient candidate without an authored target-proof word.</p><p>The source-family proofs are existing checked infrastructure and overlap this theorem family. This result therefore demonstrates automatic recomposition of known bodies, rather than discovery of new lemmas or an unseen theorem family. The grammar permits at most two components and one canonical embedding per binding; it remains a restricted cluster control.</p><p>The markings encode fixed formula and reference constraints. They are not learned geometric failure markings. No RL policy was trained or queried, and no native checker was invoked. Universal first-order encoding, arithmetic transfer, learned cluster construction, practical regions and movable boundaries, and turtle/Penrose experiments remain active tasks.</p></section>'
    checked_words=('The independent run reconstructs all '+math(disposition['events'])+' events, all '+math(disposition['complete_graph_states'])+' reached complete point graphs and '+math(disposition['base_binding_checks'])+' literal candidate bindings. It verifies the '+math(disposition['primitive_rows'])+'-row primitive proof and the flattened request retaining the original hypotheses, with no lemma blocks. All '+math(disposition['actual_payload_controls_rejected'])+' altered event payloads differ from independently reconstructed templates; all '+math(disposition['actual_mutated_certificate_or_symbolic_controls_rejected'])+' mutated complete certificates or symbolic proofs are actually rejected by independent checker calls. Event controls are not full mutated-tape replays. This positive tape has no failed branch or rollback event.') if accepted else html.escape(disposition['human_summary'])
    page+='<section class="panel" id="checks"><h2>Separate discovery from checking.</h2><p>'+checked_words+'</p><p>The saved positive candidate certificate retains all '+math(24)+' primitive rows and the original context. The flattened request has no lemma blocks. Independent checking must verify rule licenses, ordered prior references, exact full placement identities, unit occupancy, every assigned marking, and the final target. Displaying the rows is not itself a validity check.</p><p>Mutation controls, when executed, are individually scoped in their raw audit record. They do not automatically establish full altered-tape or owner replay coverage. The exact frozen JSON files define parser scope.</p></section>'
    page+='<section class="panel" id="parallel"><h2>Parallel agents with one execution owner.</h2><div class="tracks"><article><h3>Arithmetic and learning</h3><p>Policy mathematics, arithmetic transfer and independent prospective source review. A frozen numeric fixture gate is ready; this phase does not execute training.</p></article><article><h3>Hilbert geometry</h3><p>Independent point, trace and symbolic-certificate sources, with a separately owned actual audit.</p></article><article><h3>Search and controls</h3><p>The fixed-pool adapter and exact saved comparisons with the primitive and receptor controls.</p></article></div><p>ROOT reviews and activates actual runs, owns their terminal handles, integrates the evidence and publishes. Independent agents can work concurrently without sharing authority to admit a proof.</p></section>'
    page+='<section class="panel" id="cost"><h2>Retain construction and checking costs.</h2>'+cost+'<p>The producer search interval is '+math(result['seconds'])+' seconds; its Controller setup '+math(result['controller_and_ordering_setup_seconds'])+' seconds and cold model/body/pool registration '+math(result['preparation_costs']['full_point_model_body_pool_decode_and_registration_seconds'])+' seconds are nested inside the longer dispatched process. Other subphase timers overlap and are not added as separate bills.</p><p>The earlier pure fixture clock of '+math('0.140686833')+' seconds is an owner pre-write interval. Its process startup and final receipt write were not measured, so the recorded total is not a complete end-to-end cost. The later preparation, static audit and this search use the preserved dispatch clocks. Unmeasured work is additional.</p><p>The producer owner peak estimate is '+math(life['conservative_host_peak_bytes'])+' bytes. The inherited monitor omits simultaneous observer RSS, so this is not a strict aggregate host upper bound. The '+math(512)+r'-MiB threshold is a sampled and retrospective acceptance gate, not a hard operating-system memory cap. The fixed '+math(170)+'-second worker, '+math(175)+'-second supervisor and '+math(180)+'-second outer time guards were retained. All producer processes were reaped normally.</p><p>ROOT metadata preflight took '+math('0.540004583')+' seconds and independent producer source metadata checks '+math('1.273712959')+' seconds; these are additional. Source reading and authoring remain unmeasured, not zero. Previous matching phases retain '+math('50.956800624')+' and '+math('50.405773542')+' owned seconds, and still earlier inventory and failed gates remain additional.</p></section>'
    page+='<section class="panel" id="evidence"><h2>Inspect the saved evidence.</h2><p>'+link(str((SOURCE/'fixed-whole-family-pool-result-v1.json.gz').relative_to(ROOT)),'Complete actual search result')+' · '+link(str((SOURCE/'search-plan-v1.json').relative_to(ROOT)),'Frozen search plan')+' · '+link(str((HERE/'search-terminal-v1.json').relative_to(ROOT)),'Full dispatch clock')+' · '+link(str((HERE/'actual-audit-disposition-v1.json').relative_to(ROOT)),'Independent acceptance disposition')+'</p><p><a href="visual-data.json">Exact viewer rows</a> · <a href="result-summary.json">Result summary</a> · <a href="origins.json">Published origins</a> · <a href="source-input-bindings.json">Exact prerequisite routes</a> · <a href="external-runtime-bindings.json">Runtime identities</a> · <a href="sources-and-inputs.zip">Additional sources and historical versions</a></p><p>The reader displays saved evidence and runs no scientific checker. Runtime binaries are excluded. Earlier notebooks preserve their historical pending states; this notebook records the new execution. The broader research goal remains active.</p></section></main><script defer src="viewer.js"></script></body></html>'
